<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 21 May, from 878 to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/aghlabid-dynasty" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aghlabid-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/878">878 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,148 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Aghlabids capture Syracuse, the Byzantine capital of Sicily</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege begun in August 877, Aghlabid forces took Syracuse, the Byzantine capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, which the central Byzantine government had effectively left without assistance. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghlabid-dynasty">Aghlabids</a> had begun their conquest of Byzantine Sicily in 827.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghlabid-dynasty">Aghlabid dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arab-byzantine-wars">Arab–Byzantine wars</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/879">879 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,147 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope John VIII blesses Duke Branimir and the Croatian people</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pope John VIII gave his blessing to Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/branimir-of-croatia">Branimir of Croatia</a>, his authority and the whole Croatian people, and confirmed it by letter on 7 June. The blessing came to be regarded as papal recognition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> as an independent state.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/branimir-of-croatia">Branimir of Croatia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">996 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,030 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Otto III is crowned Holy Roman Emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Otto III, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> since the age of three and son of Emperor Otto II and Theophanu, was crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>. Influenced by his Byzantine mother, he dreamed of renewing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Otto III</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperator-romanorum">Imperator Romanorum</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1502">1502 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">524 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Portuguese navigator João da Nova sights St Helena</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Returning from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, João da Nova's fleet found an uninhabited island in the South Atlantic, traditionally on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-helena">St Helena</a>'s feast day. It became a vital supply stop and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s place of exile.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1674">1674 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">352 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Sobieski is elected King of Poland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The nobility of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> elected the victorious commander Jan Sobieski as John III. In 1683 he led the relief army that broke the Ottoman siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1840">1840 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">186 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Hobson proclaims British sovereignty over New Zealand</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Following the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-waitangi">Treaty of Waitangi</a>, Lieutenant-Governor Hobson declared British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over the North Island by cession and the South Island by discovery. The treaty's meaning is still central to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1881">1881 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">145 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Clara Barton founds the American Red Cross</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Clara Barton, a nurse in the Civil War, set up the American Association of the Red Cross in Washington. It became the country's main organisation for disaster relief and blood donation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1927">1927 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">99 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lindbergh lands in Paris after flying the Atlantic alone</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles Lindbergh touched down at Le Bourget after 33.5 hours in the air, greeted by a crowd of some 100,000. He won the $25,000 Orteig Prize and instant worldwide fame.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1991">1991 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rajiv Gandhi is assassinated in Tamil Nadu</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A suicide bomber from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberation-tigers-of-tamil-eelam">Tamil Tigers</a> killed the former Indian prime minister at an election rally in Sriperumbudur. His mother, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indira-gandhi">Indira Gandhi</a>, had been assassinated in 1984.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 21 May <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/albrecht-durer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/albrecht-durer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Albrecht Dürer</span><span class="tp">1471–1528</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lucien-bonaparte"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lucien-bonaparte.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lucien Bonaparte</span><span class="tp">1775–1840</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/itagaki-taisuke"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/itagaki-taisuke.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Itagaki Taisuke</span><span class="tp">1837–1919</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-batlle-y-ordonez"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-batlle-y-ordonez.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Batlle y Ordóñez</span><span class="tp">1856–1929</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lazaro-cardenas"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lazaro-cardenas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lázaro Cárdenas</span><span class="tp">1895–1970</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 21 May <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sun-quan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sun-quan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sun Quan</span><span class="tp">182–252</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/feng-dao"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/feng-dao.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Feng Dao</span><span class="tp">882–954</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/christian-i-of-denmark"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/christian-i-of-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Christian I of Denmark</span><span class="tp">1426–1481</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pandolfo-petrucci"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pandolfo-petrucci.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pandolfo Petrucci</span><span class="tp">1452–1512</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hernando-de-soto"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hernando-de-soto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hernando de Soto</span><span class="tp">c. 1500–1542</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-eliot-missionary"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-eliot-missionary.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Eliot (missionary)</span><span class="tp">1604–1690</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/arturo-prat"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/arturo-prat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Arturo Prat</span><span class="tp">1848–1879</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/venustiano-carranza"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/venustiano-carranza.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Venustiano Carranza</span><span class="tp">1859–1920</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rajiv-gandhi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rajiv-gandhi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rajiv Gandhi</span><span class="tp">1944–1991</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
